module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjCoherentII.Truncation

/-!
# When the degree-at-least-`k` truncation of the twisted global sections is a finite module

Let `S = ⨁_{d ≥ 0} 𝒮 d` be a nonnegatively graded ring, `X = Proj 𝒮` and `ℱ` a sheaf of
`𝒪_X`-modules, and give `⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` the graded `S`-module structure of Tag 03GK. For
an integer `k` the truncation `⨁_{n ≥ k} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjCoherentII/Truncation.lean` is a finite `S`-module as soon as

* each homogeneous piece `Γ(X, ℱ(n))` generates a finitely generated `S`-submodule, and
* above some degree `B` every homogeneous piece lies in the `S`-span of the one below it.

Indeed the second hypothesis walks every piece of degree `> max k B` down into the span of the
pieces of degrees `k, …, max k B`, finitely many of which are finitely generated by the first.

This is the bookkeeping half of the sandwich in the proof of [Stacks, Tag 01YS] clause (5): the
source sandwiches `M_k = ⨁_{d ≥ k} H⁰(ℙⁿ_R, ℱ(d))` between two finite modules, and what it uses
of the geometry is exactly the two hypotheses above — degreewise finiteness over the coefficient
ring, which is clause (3) at `i = 0`, and generation of the high degrees in degree one, which is
what the surjection from a finite direct sum of twists provides once the first cohomology of its
kernel vanishes.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistedSections.twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation_eq_iSup`: the
  truncation is the supremum of the spans of the homogeneous pieces in degrees `k, …, max k B`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistedSections`
  `.fg_span_twistedGlobalSectionsGrading_of_span_eq_top`: the first hypothesis holds for a degree
  whose section group is generated by finitely many sections over a ring acting through the
  degree-preserving scalars — on `ℙⁿ_R` the coefficients `R` acting through the constants.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistedSections.fg_twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation`: the
  truncation is a finitely generated `S`-submodule.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistedSections.moduleFinite_twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation`:
  the same, read as `Module.Finite`.

## Implementation notes

The walk down is an induction with `Int.le_induction` on the degree, starting at `k`: a piece of
degree `d + 1` is either still inside the finite window, or `d + 1 > B`, in which case the step
hypothesis puts it in the span of the degree-`d` piece, which the induction hypothesis has
already placed inside the window's span.

The finite window is indexed by `Finset.Icc k B'` with `B' = max k B` rather than by `Set.Icc`,
so that `Submodule.fg_iSup` applies with the finiteness of the index type coming from the
`Finset` coercion.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01YS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01YS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03GK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03GK)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace DirectSum
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj
  (twistSheafOfModules twistedGlobalSections)
open scoped Stacks.GradedLocalization

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistedSections

universe u w

attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top
attribute [local implicit_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf sheafCompose AlgebraicGeometry.Proj

variable {S : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing S] [SetLike σ S] [AddSubgroupClass σ S]
  (𝒮 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒮]

variable (F : SheafOfModules.{u}
  ((sheafCompose (Opens.grothendieckTopology (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒮))
    (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})).obj
      (ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.structureSheaf 𝒮)))

variable [Module S (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F)]
  (hsmul : ∀ (i : ℕ) (n : ℤ) (a : 𝒮 i) (s : twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F n),
    (a : S) • (DirectSum.of (fun m : ℤ => twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F m) n s :
        twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F) =
      DirectSum.of (fun m : ℤ => twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F m) ((i : ℤ) + n)
        (homogeneousScalarTwistedSections 𝒮 F i n a s))

/-- The `S`-span of the homogeneous twisted global sections of the degrees in a finite window. -/
def truncationWindow (k B : ℤ) : Submodule S (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F) :=
  ⨆ m : Finset.Icc k (max k B),
    Submodule.span S (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F (m : ℤ) :
      Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F))

/-- **The high degrees walk down into the window.** If every homogeneous piece of degree `> B`
lies in the `S`-span of the piece one degree below, then every homogeneous piece of degree
`≥ k` lies in the span of the pieces of degrees `k, …, max k B`. -/
theorem coe_twistedGlobalSectionsGrading_subset_truncationWindow (k B : ℤ)
    (hstep : ∀ d : ℤ, B < d →
      (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F d : Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F)) ⊆
        Submodule.span S (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F (d - 1) :
          Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F)))
    (d : ℤ) (hd : k ≤ d) :
    (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F d : Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F)) ⊆
      truncationWindow 𝒮 F k B := by
  have hwin : ∀ m : ℤ, k ≤ m → m ≤ max k B →
      (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F m : Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F)) ⊆
        truncationWindow 𝒮 F k B :=
    fun m hm hmB => Submodule.subset_span.trans
      (le_iSup (fun j : Finset.Icc k (max k B) =>
        Submodule.span S (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F (j : ℤ) :
          Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F)))
        ⟨m, Finset.mem_Icc.mpr ⟨hm, hmB⟩⟩)
  induction d, hd using Int.leInduction with
  | base => exact hwin k le_rfl (le_max_left _ _)
  | succ d hd ih =>
    rcases le_or_gt (d + 1) (max k B) with hle | hgt
    · exact hwin (d + 1) (by omega) hle
    · have hB : B < d + 1 := by
        have := le_max_right k B
        omega
      refine (hstep (d + 1) hB).trans (Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_)
      simpa using ih

include hsmul in
/-- **The truncation is the span of the window.** Under the step hypothesis the degree-`≥ k`
truncation of the twisted global sections is generated by the homogeneous pieces of degrees
`k, …, max k B`. -/
theorem twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation_eq_iSup (k B : ℤ)
    (hstep : ∀ d : ℤ, B < d →
      (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F d : Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F)) ⊆
        Submodule.span S (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F (d - 1) :
          Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F))) :
    twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation 𝒮 F hsmul k = truncationWindow 𝒮 F k B := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation_eq_span 𝒮 F hsmul k]
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr (Set.iUnion₂_subset fun m hm => ?_)
    exact coe_twistedGlobalSectionsGrading_subset_truncationWindow 𝒮 F k B hstep m
      (Set.mem_Ici.mp hm)
  · refine iSup_le fun m => Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_
    exact coe_twistedGlobalSectionsGrading_subset_truncation 𝒮 F hsmul k (m : ℤ)
      (Finset.mem_Icc.mp m.2).1

/-- **A finite generating family of one section group spans the corresponding homogeneous
piece.** If the coefficients `R` act on `Γ(X, ℱ(d))` through a map `ι : R → S` compatible with
the graded action — `ι r • (s in degree d) = (r • s) in degree d` — and finitely many sections
generate `Γ(X, ℱ(d))` over `R`, then the degree-`d` homogeneous piece of
`⨁_{m ∈ ℤ} Γ(X, ℱ(m))` spans a finitely generated `S`-submodule. -/
theorem fg_span_twistedGlobalSectionsGrading_of_span_eq_top (d : ℤ)
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [Module R (twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F d)] (ι : R → S)
    (hι : ∀ (r : R) (s : twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F d),
      ι r • (DirectSum.of (fun m : ℤ => twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F m) d s :
          twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F) =
        DirectSum.of (fun m : ℤ => twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F m) d (r • s))
    (t : Finset (twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F d))
    (ht : Submodule.span R (t : Set (twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F d)) = ⊤) :
    (Submodule.span S (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F d :
      Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F))).FG := by
  classical
  refine ⟨t.image (DirectSum.of (fun m : ℤ => twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F m) d),
    le_antisymm (Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_) (Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_)⟩
  · intro x hx
    simp only [Finset.coe_image, Set.mem_image, Finset.mem_coe] at hx
    obtain ⟨i, -, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact Submodule.subset_span
      ((DirectSum.mem_rangeGrading ℤ (fun m : ℤ => twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F m) d _).mpr
        ⟨i, rfl⟩)
  · intro x hx
    obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ :=
      (DirectSum.mem_rangeGrading ℤ (fun m : ℤ => twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F m) d x).mp hx
    have hs : s ∈ Submodule.span R (t : Set (twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F d)) := by
      rw [ht]; exact Submodule.mem_top
    obtain ⟨c, -, hc⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_finset.mp hs
    have hsum : (DirectSum.of (fun m : ℤ => twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F m) d s :
          twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F) =
        ∑ i ∈ t, ι (c i) •
          (DirectSum.of (fun m : ℤ => twistedSectionsComponent 𝒮 F m) d i :
            twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F) := by
      rw [← hc, map_sum]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => (hι (c i) i).symm
    rw [hsum]
    exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i hi => Submodule.smul_mem _ _
      (Submodule.subset_span (Finset.mem_coe.mpr (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hi)))

include hsmul in
/-- **The degree-`≥ k` truncation of the twisted global sections is a finitely generated
`S`-module**, provided each homogeneous piece spans a finitely generated submodule and the
pieces above degree `B` are spanned by the pieces below them. -/
theorem fg_twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation (k B : ℤ)
    (hfg : ∀ d : ℤ, (Submodule.span S (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F d :
      Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F))).FG)
    (hstep : ∀ d : ℤ, B < d →
      (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F d : Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F)) ⊆
        Submodule.span S (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F (d - 1) :
          Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F))) :
    (twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation 𝒮 F hsmul k).FG := by
  rw [twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation_eq_iSup 𝒮 F hsmul k B hstep]
  exact Submodule.fg_iSup _ fun m => hfg (m : ℤ)

include hsmul in
/-- **The degree-`≥ k` truncation of the twisted global sections is a finite `S`-module**, in
the `Module.Finite` spelling. -/
theorem moduleFinite_twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation (k B : ℤ)
    (hfg : ∀ d : ℤ, (Submodule.span S (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F d :
      Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F))).FG)
    (hstep : ∀ d : ℤ, B < d →
      (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F d : Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F)) ⊆
        Submodule.span S (twistedGlobalSectionsGrading 𝒮 F (d - 1) :
          Set (twistedGlobalSections 𝒮 F))) :
    Module.Finite S (twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation 𝒮 F hsmul k) :=
  Module.Finite.iff_fg.mpr (fg_twistedGlobalSectionsTruncation 𝒮 F hsmul k B hfg hstep)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistedSections

end
